Subject: [PATCH] Exynos8895: avoid UFS MMIO after shutdown isolation

The SM-G955N shutdown trace aborts when exynos_ufs_setup_clocks reads
HCI_CLKSTOP_CTRL after link-off and PHY isolation. At this point the
core has already disabled its clocks. Skip the late vendor register
access on Exynos8895 while leaving the earlier PHY and host shutdown
sequence in place. Keep the normal suspend/resume path unchanged.

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
@@ -1054,6 +1054,15 @@
 			exynos_ufs_disable_auto_ctrl_hcc(ufs);
 		exynos_ufs_ungate_clks(ufs);
 	} else if (!on && status == POST_CHANGE) {
+		/*
+		 * On Exynos8895 the PHY has already been isolated when
+		 * shutdown drops the host clocks. HCI_CLKSTOP_CTRL and
+		 * HCI_MISC cannot be accessed here.
+		 */
+		if (ufs->drv_data->native_hibern8_status &&
+		    hba->shutting_down && ufshcd_is_link_off(hba))
+			return 0;
+
 		exynos_ufs_gate_clks(ufs);
 		if (ufs->opts & EXYNOS_UFS_OPT_BROKEN_AUTO_CLK_CTRL)
 			exynos_ufs_enable_auto_ctrl_hcc(ufs);
